  "worked_solution": "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{11}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{11}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{40}{15}+\\frac{33}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{30}.$",
